</style></head><body><main>
<div class="eyebrow">Gojo · native ornament experiments</div><h1>What must stay, what usually stays, and what is free</h1>
<p class="intro">The same idea can admit many drawings. Here, the evidence stays fixed while the question changes: some observations become requirements, some guide a default realization, and others are deliberately left unused.</p>
<div class="nav"><a href="overview.html">All 72 constructions</a><a href="../ornament-concepts/gallery.html">Branch-and-route concepts</a><a href="../ornament-reconstruction/gallery.html">Reconstruction study</a></div>
<div class="principles"><div class="principle"><strong>Requirements define the contract</strong><span>A contradiction excludes a candidate. An unavailable required read remains unresolved.</span></div><div class="principle"><strong>Defaults guide a realization</strong><span>Unusual aspect, retracing or unexplained contact can lower preference without making the concept false.</span></div><div class="principle"><strong>Unused is a real choice</strong><span>Omitted symmetry or count is not secretly enforced. A waiver leaves the original evidence visible.</span></div></div>
<div class="controls"><label>Construction family<select id="family"></select></label><label>Read context or a single policy change<select id="profile"></select></label><label>Show alternatives<select id="display"><option value="all">All constructions</option><option value="preferred">Undominated by defaults</option><option value="admissible">Still possible</option><option value="excluded">Outside required claims</option></select></label><div class="display-options"><label class="check"><input id="groups" type="checkbox">Show mechanical groups</label><label class="check"><input id="envelope" type="checkbox">Show chosen boundary</label></div></div>
<div class="context"><aside class="reference"><div class="eyebrow">Reference, not a mandatory image</div><img id="reference-image" alt="Reference construction"><div id="reference-title" class="title"></div><p id="reference-note" class="note"></p></aside><section class="policy"><h2 id="policy-title"></h2><p id="policy-note"></p><div id="summary" class="counts"></div><div class="hint">Preference is a partial order. “Undominated” can include several candidates, and unresolved default ranges can prevent a comparison. These are explicit ordinal assumptions, not measured probabilities.</div><details id="policy-details"><summary>Inspect the current 12-rule contract</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Available distinction</th><th>Authority</th><th>Expected answer</th></tr></thead><tbody id="policy-rules"></tbody></table></div></details><p class="standards">Optional finer word-basis reads use an envelope half-span of 8 shared reaches, an ordinary aspect threshold of 4, and a contour breadth resolution of 8. These are selected standards, not universal aesthetic laws. Breadth concerns declared closed mechanical contours; fill ownership is not supplied.</p></section></div>
<section id="inspection" class="inspection" hidden><div class="inspection-head"><h2 id="inspect-title"></h2><button id="close-inspection" type="button">Close comparison</button></div><p id="inspect-note" class="muted"></p><div class="comparison"><figure><figcaption>Family reference</figcaption><img id="inspect-source" alt="Reference"></figure><figure><figcaption>Candidate under the current question</figcaption><img id="inspect-target" alt="Candidate"></figure></div><p id="inspect-result" class="hint"></p><p class="scroll-hint">Swipe the table sideways to inspect expectations and policy decisions.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Native distinction</th><th>Observed fact</th><th>Expected</th><th>Authority</th><th>Policy read</th></tr></thead><tbody id="inspect-facts"></tbody></table></div></section>
<div class="catalog-head"><h2 id="family-title"></h2><p id="shown-count"></p></div><div id="cards" class="cards"></div>
<section id="signatures" class="signature"></section><section class="limits"><h2>What this read does and does not establish</h2><ul id="limits"></ul></section><footer id="run-note"></footer>
</main><script src="data.js"></script><script>
(()=>{'use strict';const d=globalThis.ORNAMENT_DEFAULTS;const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);const esc=value=>String(value??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));const tierNames=['Required','Strong default','Preference','Unused'];let selected=null;
const family=()=>d.families.find(f=>f.id===$('family').value)||d.families[0];const profiles=f=>[...f.profiles.map(p=>({...p,key:'profile/'+p.id})),...(f.interventions||[]).map(p=>({...p,key:'intervention/'+p.id}))];const profile=()=>profiles(family()).find(p=>p.key===$('profile').value)||profiles(family())[0];const image=c=>$('envelope').checked?($('groups').checked?c.envelopeGroupImage:c.envelopeImage):$('groups').checked?c.groupImage:c.image;const range=(lo,hi)=>lo===hi?String(lo):lo+'–'+hi;
function status(r){const p=profile();return r.answer==='No'?'Outside required claims':r.answer==='Blocked'?'Required read blocked':r.answer==='Open'?'Required read unresolved':p.tiers.includes(0)?'Requirements satisfied':p.id==='free'?'No required claims':'Possible under defaults'}
function authority(p,i){return p.waived.includes(i)?'Waived '+tierNames[p.tiers[i]].toLowerCase():tierNames[p.tiers[i]]}
function expectation(p,i){return p.tiers[i]===3?'Uncommitted':p.waived.includes(i)?'Waived '+(p.expected[i]?'Yes':'No'):p.expected[i]?'Yes':'No'}
function outcome(read){return({Yes:'Agrees',No:'Contradicts',Open:'Unresolved',Blocked:'Read blocked',Unused:'Carried unused',Waived:'Waived; fact retained'})[read]||read}
function burden(r){return 'Strong defaults: '+range(r.strongLower,r.strongUpper)+' departures · preferences: '+range(r.weakLower,r.weakUpper)}
function populate(){const f=family();$('profile').innerHTML='<optgroup label="Read contexts">'+f.profiles.map(p=>'<option value="profile/'+esc(p.id)+'">'+esc(p.name)+'</option>').join('')+'</optgroup>'+(f.interventions?.length?'<optgroup label="One change from ordinary defaults">'+f.interventions.map(p=>'<option value="intervention/'+esc(p.id)+'">'+esc(p.name)+'</option>').join('')+'</optgroup>':'');$('profile').value=f.profiles.some(p=>p.id==='ordinary')?'profile/ordinary':'profile/'+f.profiles[0].id;selected=null;$('inspection').hidden=true;render()}
function inspect(id,scroll=false){const f=family(),p=profile(),c=f.cases.find(c=>c.id===id),r=p.results.find(r=>r.id===id);if(!c||!r){selected=null;$('inspection').hidden=true;return}selected=id;$('inspection').hidden=false;$('inspect-title').textContent=c.id+' · '+c.name;$('inspect-note').textContent=c.constructionNote;$('inspect-source').src=image(f.cases.find(c=>c.id===f.referenceId));$('inspect-target').src=image(c);$('inspect-result').textContent=status(r)+'. '+burden(r)+'. '+(r.frontier?'Undominated under this policy.':r.eligible?'Another possible candidate may be preferred under this policy.':'Defaults cannot override a required contradiction.');$('inspect-facts').innerHTML=d.rules.map((rule,i)=>'<tr data-rule="'+i+'"><td>'+esc(rule.label)+'</td><td class="fact">'+esc(c.facts[i])+'</td><td>'+esc(expectation(p,i))+'</td><td class="tier">'+esc(authority(p,i))+'</td><td>'+esc(outcome(r.reads[i]))+'</td></tr>').join('');if(scroll)$('inspection').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'})}
function signatures(f){const s=f.signatures;if(!s){$('signatures').innerHTML='';return}const goals=s.goalIds||[];$('signatures').innerHTML='<h2>What could a smaller rule set say?</h2><p>The target here is the set admitted by the family’s complete branch-and-route question. The search tries to describe that set with a single conjunction of other available distinctions, using the observed reference polarities and excluding the whole-arrangement answer itself.</p><p><strong>'+(s.exactPossible?'An exact separating conjunction exists in this finite corpus.':'No single conjunction of the tested reference cues exactly separates this target set.')+'</strong> '+esc(s.checked)+' combinations checked. '+esc(goals.length)+' target constructions.</p><p class="muted">'+esc(s.note)+'</p><div class="solutions">'+s.solutions.slice(0,8).map((solution,n)=>'<article class="solution"><strong>'+esc(solution.rules.length)+' clauses · '+esc(solution.participants)+' native participants</strong><p>'+solution.rules.map((rule,i)=>esc(d.rules[rule].label)+' = <b>'+esc(solution.expected[i]?'Yes':'No')+'</b>').join('; ')+'</p><p>Admits: <code>'+esc(solution.accepted.join(', ')||'none')+'</code></p><p>Admits outside target: <code>'+esc(solution.falseAccepted.join(', ')||'none')+'</code><br>Excludes target alternatives: <code>'+esc(solution.falseExcluded.join(', ')||'none')+'</code></p></article>').join('')+'</div><p class="standards">The search minimizes clause count and classification tradeoffs within this corpus; native participant cost is reported separately. This is not a universal minimum, learned probability or complete definition of the ornament.</p>'}
function render(){const f=family(),p=profile(),ref=f.cases.find(c=>c.id===f.referenceId);$('reference-image').src=image(ref);$('reference-title').textContent=ref.id+' · '+ref.name;$('reference-note').textContent=f.repertoireNote;$('policy-title').textContent=p.name;$('policy-note').textContent=p.note;$('family-title').textContent=f.name;const eligible=p.results.filter(r=>r.eligible),frontier=p.results.filter(r=>r.frontier),excluded=p.results.filter(r=>!r.eligible);$('summary').innerHTML=[[eligible.length,'still possible'],[frontier.length,'undominated'],[excluded.length,'outside required claims']].map(([n,label])=>'<div class="count"><strong>'+n+'</strong><span>'+label+'</span></div>').join('');$('policy-rules').innerHTML=d.rules.map((rule,i)=>'<tr data-rule="'+i+'"><td>'+esc(rule.label)+'<br><small>'+esc(rule.note)+'</small></td><td>'+esc(authority(p,i))+'</td><td>'+esc(expectation(p,i))+'</td></tr>').join('');const display=$('display').value;const showing=f.cases.filter(c=>{const r=p.results.find(r=>r.id===c.id);return display==='all'||display==='preferred'&&r.frontier||display==='admissible'&&r.eligible||display==='excluded'&&!r.eligible});$('shown-count').textContent=showing.length+' of '+f.cases.length+' constructions shown';$('cards').innerHTML=showing.length?showing.map(c=>{const r=p.results.find(r=>r.id===c.id);return '<article data-target="'+esc(c.id)+'" class="card '+(!r.eligible?'excluded':r.answer==='Open'?'open':'')+'"><div class="card-head"><h3><span class="id">'+esc(c.id)+'</span>'+esc(c.name)+'</h3><span class="pill">'+esc(status(r))+'</span></div><img loading="lazy" src="'+esc(image(c))+'" alt="'+esc(c.name)+'"><div class="card-body"><p class="note">'+esc(c.constructionNote)+'</p><p class="burden">'+esc(burden(r))+'<br><span class="'+(r.frontier?'frontier':'muted')+'">'+(r.frontier?'Undominated under this policy':r.eligible?'Still possible; defaults may prefer another realization':'Required evidence does not agree')+'</span></p><button type="button" class="inspect" data-inspect="'+esc(c.id)+'">Inspect facts and rule decisions</button></div></article>'}).join(''):'<p class="empty">No constructions meet this display filter under the selected contract.</p>';$('cards').querySelectorAll('[data-inspect]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>inspect(button.dataset.inspect,true)));signatures(f);if(selected)inspect(selected);globalThis.ORNAMENT_DEFAULTS_VIEW={family:f.id,profile:p.key,display,groups:$('groups').checked,envelope:$('envelope').checked}}
$('family').innerHTML=d.families.map(f=>'<option value="'+esc(f.id)+'">'+esc(f.name)+'</option>').join('');const params=new URLSearchParams(location.search);if(d.families.some(f=>f.id===params.get('family')))$('family').value=params.get('family');$('family').addEventListener('change',populate);for(const id of ['profile','display','groups','envelope'])$(id).addEventListener('change',render);$('close-inspection').addEventListener('click',()=>{selected=null;$('inspection').hidden=true});$('limits').innerHTML=d.limits.map(limit=>'<li>'+esc(limit)+'</li>').join('');$('run-note').textContent=d.counts.designs+' native constructions · '+d.counts.families+' presentation families · '+d.counts.rules+' available distinctions · '+Number(d.counts.policyReads).toLocaleString()+' policy reads. Independent native execution supplies the drawings; labels never decide admission.';populate();if(params.has('case'))inspect(params.get('case'));
})();
</script></body></html>
""";

    private static string Overview() => """
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Ornament defaults · construction overview</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f5f3eb;color:#24444b;font:15px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1800px;margin:auto;padding:25px}h1,h2,h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:500}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin:30px 0 12px;font-size:26px}h3{font-size:17px;margin:0;padding:10px 12px}p{max-width:980px}a{color:#2d6470}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}.card{border:1px solid #ccd5ce;background:#fffdf6;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden;min-width:0}.card img{display:block;width:100%;height:160px;object-fit:contain}.card p{font-size:12px;color:#6b7775;margin:0;padding:8px 12px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#677a78}.id{font:11px system-ui,sans-serif;color:#75827e;display:block}footer{font-size:13px;margin-top:25px;color:#6b7775}@media(max-width:1300px){.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:850px){.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:550px){main{padding:18px 12px}.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:8px}.card img{height:120px}h1{font-size:29px}}</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">Gojo · counterfactual construction atlas</div><h1>One repertoire, many possible contracts</h1><p>All 72 native constructions, including ordinary alternatives, different mechanical recipes, unusual proportions and deliberately conflicting contacts. These are candidates to inspect, not 72 endorsed ornament designs. Family names organize this page; native questions decide whether a candidate fits.</p><p><a href="gallery.html">Explore requirements, defaults and minimal descriptions</a></p><div id="families"></div><footer>Each line is an observed segment emitted by an executable Gojo recipe. Display coordinates and names do not decide its interpretation.</footer></main><script src="data.js"></script><script>(()=>{const d=globalThis.ORNAMENT_DEFAULTS,esc=v=>String(v??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));document.getElementById('families').innerHTML=d.families.map(f=>'<section data-family="'+esc(f.id)+'"><h2>'+esc(f.name)+'</h2><p>'+esc(f.repertoireNote)+'</p><div class="cards">'+f.cases.map(c=>'<a class="card" href="gallery.html?family='+encodeURIComponent(f.id)+'&amp;case='+encodeURIComponent(c.id)+'"><h3><span class="id">'+esc(c.id)+'</span>'+esc(c.name)+'</h3><img loading="lazy" src="'+esc(c.image)+'" alt="'+esc(c.name)+'"><p>'+esc(c.constructionNote)+'</p></a>').join('')+'</div></section>').join('')})()</script></body></html>
""";
